        <briefdescription>
<para>Distributes a budget of <emphasis>maxSampledPoints</emphasis> across <emphasis>runs</emphasis>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns one sampled count per run. Runs with fewer than two samples receive zero (they cannot form an area). Every other run keeps at least its first and last data point, so the total may exceed the budget by at most two data points per run when a curve contains very many gaps. </para>
